# Exclude bazzite-fork (has symlinks that break on Windows)
bazzite-fork/

# Exclude containers build files (has symlinks that break on Windows)
containers/system_files/
containers/build_files/

# Git
.git/

# Never bake credentials into published images.
# The Containerfile's staging stage bundles a `git archive HEAD` snapshot at
# /usr/lib/powos/src (built as .snapshot/ in CI). `git archive` already
# excludes .git and respects .gitattributes, but anything the workflow
# happens to add to the checkout WOULD ship — belt-and-suspenders:
secrets/
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Build artifacts
build/output/
*.raw
*.iso
*.img

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Temp
*.tmp
*.log

# ── Context bulk that no COPY ever reads ──────────────────────────
#
# `podman build` tars and hashes the whole context before it runs the first
# instruction, so anything here is paid for on EVERY build including a fully
# cached one. Measured on this tree: extensions/ 355M + bazzite/ 128M = 483M of
# the 490M context, and grep says no COPY in the Containerfile names either.
#
# bazzite/ is vendored by build/vendor-bazzite.sh for a `COPY bazzite/system_files/`
# that the Containerfile no longer has. The vendor step still exists for other
# consumers; excluding the directory here does not remove it, it stops the image
# build from carrying it. If a COPY of it ever comes back, delete this line —
# build/iterate.sh greps for exactly that and fails loudly if the two disagree.
extensions/
bazzite/

# Multi-GB KDE source clone cache. The Containerfile comment already says it is
# "never part of the build context"; that was true only because it happened to
# be absent, not because anything enforced it.
sources/*/upstream/

# Tier bookkeeping (raw cache key, gate record, timings). build/output/ is
# already excluded above under "Build artifacts".
build/.cache/
